# Required. Connection string for a Neon Postgres database (or any Postgres
# reachable over HTTP-compatible driver). Create a free project at
# https://neon.tech, then copy its pooled connection string here.
DATABASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The model. Set ONE of the two keys below — Atlas talks to whichever it finds.
#
# Six behaviours use it: role classification, the findings narrative, reading
# the upload instructions into an ingest plan, reading the hypothesis layer
# into business facts, reconciling two brand vocabularies, and reading an org
# chart out of an image or a scanned PDF.
#
# The first five have a deterministic fallback and run on it — visibly, never
# silently — when no key is set. The sixth does not: a picture has no honest
# deterministic reading, so those files are refused with a reason. Everything
# else works, including PDFs with a text layer, which is most of them.
#
# Nothing here ever produces a number a client sees. Every cost, ratio,
# comparison and saving is arithmetic over the establishment either way.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Which provider to use when both keys are present. Without it,
# OpenAI wins, then Anthropic, then Gemini — a deployment that has just had a
# new key added alongside an old one is a deployment that is switching, and
# making you delete the old key first would mean an outage in between.
# AI_PROVIDER=openai

# Optional model overrides. The defaults are the workhorse of each family
# rather than the newest thing, because this has to run on whatever account
# the key came from, and a model id the account cannot reach fails at the
# first request with an error that looks nothing like "wrong model".
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional fallback vendor. If the primary key above throws at call time —
# an outage, a rate limit, an account with no credit left — `ask()` retries
# the identical request against Gemini before giving up, rather than that
# outage taking down every AI-shaped behaviour in the app at once. A Gemini
# key on its own, with neither of the two above set, also works standalone.
#
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GEMINI_API_KEY=
